From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:45:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't start AEAD scatterlists with a zero-length
 entry

libspdm_aead_prealloced() and libspdm_aead() always put the associated data
first in the source and destination scatterlists, also when there is none.
<crypto/aead.h> doesn't allow zero-length entries in the used part of the
lists, and the generic gcm template indeed hashes no ciphertext then: the
ciphertext is right but the tag is wrong. With Confidential Computing on,
memmgrVerifyGspDmaOps() then fails with NV_ERR_INVALID_DATA whenever gcm(aes)
resolves to gcm_base(ctr(aes-generic),ghash-generic) (AES-NI implementations
aren't affected).

Without associated data, start the lists at the text, or at the tag if there
is no text either.

Fixes upstream issue 1448.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/libspdm_aead.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/libspdm_aead.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/libspdm_aead.c
index df3fb158..9684fc74 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/libspdm_aead.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/libspdm_aead.c
@@ -145,6 +145,19 @@ static int lkca_aead_internal(struct crypto_aead *aead,
         return -EINVAL;
     }
 
+    /*
+     * Zero-length scatterlist entries aren't allowed in the used part of an
+     * AEAD scatterlist: without associated data, the lists have to start at
+     * the text, or at the tag if there is no text either. The generic gcm
+     * template otherwise computes a wrong tag.
+     */
+    if (a_data_size == 0) {
+        int first = (data_in_size == 0) ? SG_AEAD_SIG : SG_AEAD_TEXT;
+
+        sg_in = &sg_in[first];
+        sg_out = &sg_out[first];
+    }
+
     aead_request_set_ad(req, a_data_size);
 
     aead_request_set_callback(req, CRYPTO_TFM_REQ_MAY_BACKLOG |
